{:title "Workspaces"
 :description "Scope your workflows, resources, and defaults to a project directory"
 :order 10
 :sections
 [{:heading "Quick start"
   :level 2
   :body [[:p "A workspace ties everything to one project directory: workflows, resources, default model, default provider. Initialize one and every command knows where it is."]
          [:code {:lang "bash"} "# Scaffold a workspace in your project\nglitch workspace init ~/Projects/my-project\n\n# Add a git repo as a declared resource\nglitch workspace add https://github.com/acme/backend --pin main\n\n# Make it active so every command auto-resolves it\nglitch workspace use my-project\n\n# Check status\nglitch workspace status"]]}
  {:heading "The workspace.glitch file"
   :level 2
   :body [[:p "Your workspace is declared in a single s-expression file at the root of your project:"]
          [:code {:lang "clojure"} "(workspace \"my-project\"\n  :description \"Platform command center\"\n\n  (defaults\n    :model \"qwen3-8b\"\n    :provider \"lmstudio\"\n    :elasticsearch \"http://localhost:9200\"\n    (params\n      :repo \"acme/backend\"\n      :env \"staging\"))\n\n  (resource \"backend\"\n    :type \"git\"\n    :url \"https://github.com/acme/backend\"\n    :ref \"main\"\n    :pin \"abc123def456...\")\n\n  (resource \"notes\"\n    :type \"local\"\n    :path \"~/notes\"))"]
          [:p "A minimal workspace is just a name:"]
          [:code {:lang "clojure"} "(workspace \"scratch\")"]]}
  {:heading "Defaults"
   :level 2
   :body [[:p "Set your default model, provider, Elasticsearch URL, and params once. Every workflow in the workspace inherits them:"]
          [:code {:lang "clojure"} "(defaults\n  :model \"qwen3-8b\"\n  :provider \"lmstudio\"\n  :elasticsearch \"http://localhost:9200\"\n  (params\n    :repo \"acme/backend\"\n    :team \"platform\"))"]
          [:p "Workflows use " [:code "~param.repo"] " and " [:code "~param.team"] " without " [:code "--set"] " flags. Explicit " [:code "--set"] " on the command line overrides workspace defaults."]]}
  {:heading "Resource types"
   :level 2
   :body [[:p "Three resource types, each declared inside your workspace file:"]
          [:p [:strong "git"] " -- cloned under " [:code "<workspace>/resources/<name>/"] ", pinned to a SHA. Requires " [:code ":url"] " and " [:code ":ref"] "."]
          [:p [:strong "local"] " -- symlink at " [:code "<workspace>/resources/<name>"] " pointing to an expanded path. Requires " [:code ":path"] "."]
          [:p [:strong "tracker"] " -- named alias only, no filesystem entry. Requires " [:code ":repo"] " (org/name). Useful when you reference a GitHub repo by name but don't need its code checked out."]]}
  {:heading "Referencing resources from workflows"
   :level 2
   :body [[:p "Resources are exposed via " [:code "~resource.<name>.<field>"] " template bindings:"]
          [:code {:lang "clojure"} "(step \"backend-status\"\n  (run \"cd ~resource.backend.path && git status --short\"))\n\n(step \"tracker-info\"\n  (run \"gh repo view ~resource.ops-tracker.repo\"))"]
          [:p "Available fields: " [:code ".path"] ", " [:code ".url"] ", " [:code ".ref"] ", " [:code ".pin"] ", " [:code ".repo"] ". Missing resources evaluate to empty string."]]}
  {:heading "Workspace discovery"
   :level 2
   :body [[:p "When you run any command, glitch picks a workspace using this precedence (first match wins):"]
          [:p "1. " [:code "--workspace <path>"] " flag"]
          [:p "2. " [:code "GLITCH_WORKSPACE"] " env var"]
          [:p "3. Walk up from " [:code "$PWD"] " looking for " [:code "workspace.glitch"]]
          [:p "4. Active workspace (last " [:code "glitch workspace use"] ")"]
          [:p "5. Global mode -- no workspace, CWD-relative results"]
          [:p "In practice: run " [:code "glitch workspace use my-project"] " once and every command from any directory uses that workspace until you switch."]]}
  {:heading "Directory layout"
   :level 2
   :body [[:code {:lang "text"} "~/Projects/my-project/\n+-- workspace.glitch           # config: name, defaults, resources\n+-- workflows/                 # scoped workflows\n+-- resources/                 # materialized resources (clones, symlinks)\n|   +-- backend/               # git clone\n|   +-- notes/                 # symlink to ~/notes\n+-- results/                   # run outputs\n+-- .glitch/\n    +-- glitch.db              # local run database\n    +-- .gitignore"]
          [:p "Workflows resolve from " [:code "<workspace>/workflows/"] " only. Global workflows are skipped in workspace mode."]]}
  {:heading "CLI commands"
   :level 2
   :body [[:code {:lang "bash"} "glitch workspace init [path]      # scaffold a workspace\nglitch workspace use <name>       # set active workspace\nglitch workspace list             # list registered workspaces\nglitch workspace status           # show active workspace + resources\nglitch workspace add <url|path>   # add a resource (type inferred)\nglitch workspace rm <name>        # remove a resource\nglitch workspace sync [name...]   # update resources to declared refs\nglitch workspace pin <name> <ref> # set ref, sync, write pin"]]}]}
